              "label": "Expand a list or dictionary into function-call arguments",
              "summary": "A function accepts x and y and prints each value. Rather than pass two list elements through separate indexing expressions, a call uses * to expand the list [21, 75] into positional arguments. The function receives x as 21 and y as 75. A second call uses ** to expand a dictionary containing x: 5 and y: 6 into keyword arguments, producing the corresponding values.",
              "fact_ids": [
